      "sourceTextSha256": "e0292280eaab2fc15d157abfaf04aecdf89abeda7872a5923244b36d95671e77",
      "text": "After breakfast, the group will go rafting on the Upper Napo River, better known as the Jatunyacu. In Kichwa, its name means ‘great water’.\n\nThe river alternates between big waves and rapids and calmer stretches. The route runs through the jungle and suits beginners and experienced rafters alike. No previous rafting experience is required.\n\nThe Jatunyacu is part of the headwaters of the river system that goes on to form the Amazon. After rafting, have lunch and return to the hotel.",
